  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/B4_FindingThatIsAlsoADiagnosis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE B4 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: something that is both a FindingClass and a Diagnosis</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The node types are declared disjoint. This is what stops a named cyst drifting between the two layers, which 02-modeling-case-cyst.md raises as an open question. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Nba6aab708e67422e868d91831bffdd9d"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group B] expect: unsatisfiable. The node types are declared disjoint. This is what stops a named cyst drifting between the two layers, which 02-modeling-case-cyst.md raises as an open question.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
