  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E8_PartSolidWithItsSolidComponent">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E8 [EXPECT EQUIVALENT to an existing class - yellow row in Equivalent To, does NOT move in the tree]: a part-solid nodule whose component is solid</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The resolution B1 rules out on one entity. A report saying 'part-solid nodule with a 4 mm solid component' states both values, and they are consistent because they sit on two entities: the nodule is part-solid, its component is solid. Attenuation is functional and its values are disjoint, so this only works because hasComponent supplies the second entity. Read together with B1: one entity cannot hold both, two can, and the component edge is what makes them two. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N54576884d4e644eab1d9a37965a5a1f1"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: SATISFIABLE. The resolution B1 rules out on one entity. A report saying 'part-solid nodule with a 4 mm solid component' states both values, and they are consistent because they sit on two entities: the nodule is part-solid, its component is solid. Attenuation is functional and its values are disjoint, so this only works because hasComponent supplies the second entity. Read together with B1: one entity cannot hold both, two can, and the component edge is what makes them two.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Na770720e354b46c19ed234276ebe2aa1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/scopedToRegion"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/anatomy/RID205"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/B1_SolidAndPartSolid">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE B1 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: a nodule that is both solid and part-solid</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. Value disjointness. Without it, a single-select element is single-select only by convention. Note this bites through someValuesFrom because the value classes are disjoint, not because of any cardinality axiom. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Nd38c3ded00ac4d13a2f8b60bdb89e032"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group B] expect: unsatisfiable. Value disjointness. Without it, a single-select element is single-select only by convention. Note this bites through someValuesFrom because the value classes are disjoint, not because of any cardinality axiom.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E9_BothValuesStatedResolveToTheSubtype">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E9 [EXPECT EQUIVALENT to an existing class - yellow row in Equivalent To, does NOT move in the tree]: a pulmonary nodule with part-solid attenuation and a solid component</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The full path. Asserted at the parent class with both attenuation values present, one on the nodule and one on its component. It must stay satisfiable AND classify into the part-solid subtype. E8 shows the two values coexist; this shows the coexistence does not block the classification that A3 performs. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N657d38cca5094678b8a62920a68bcb4c"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: subsumed by PartSolidPulmonaryNodule. The full path. Asserted at the parent class with both attenuation values present, one on the nodule and one on its component. It must stay satisfiable AND classify into the part-solid subtype. E8 shows the two values coexist; this shows the coexistence does not block the classification that A3 performs.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/A5_NoduleInThyroidLobe">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE A5 [EXPECT SUBCLASS of an existing class - yellow row in SubClass Of, moves in the tree when the dropdown is set to Inferred]: a nodule in the left lobe of the thyroid gland</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. Same mechanism in a second organ, to check the pattern is not lung-specific. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N74799b1f3d5e4ffcb0791a37c6d6f461"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group A] expect: subsumed by ThyroidNodule. Same mechanism in a second organ, to check the pattern is not lung-specific.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Nfc61692891474d839efe9f68a89c89c4">
