  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E5_MultiSelectAllowsTwoValues">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E5 [EXPECT CONSISTENT and nothing further - stays where it is, no yellow rows]: a pulmonary nodule with popcorn and punctate calcification</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The counterpart to B1. Calcification is deliberately multi-select, so two patterns co-occurring must remain satisfiable. If this goes red, something has declared the element functional and a lesion can no longer carry two calcification patterns. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Nb65712cd7c654d78ad1a383afc16296d"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: SATISFIABLE. The counterpart to B1. Calcification is deliberately multi-select, so two patterns co-occurring must remain satisfiable. If this goes red, something has declared the element functional and a lesion can no longer carry two calcification patterns.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
