  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/A4_NoduleInLocalSubpleuralRegion">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE A4 [EXPECT SUBCLASS of an existing class - yellow row in SubClass Of, moves in the tree when the dropdown is set to Inferred]: a nodule in the locally coined subpleural region</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The scope path runs through two locally authored partOf edges before it reaches imported RadLex structure. Tests that local gap-fill edges participate in closure. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N87c5b48550c24ba08b4fcdb79d4b7b8e"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group A] expect: subsumed by PulmonaryNodule. The scope path runs through two locally authored partOf edges before it reaches imported RadLex structure. Tests that local gap-fill edges participate in closure.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
