  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/A3_PartSolidByAttenuation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE A3 [EXPECT EQUIVALENT to an existing class - yellow row in Equivalent To, does NOT move in the tree]: a pulmonary nodule whose attenuation is part-solid</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The condition-versus-subtype case. The subtype is defined, so nobody authors it twice and the component requirement attaches to it automatically. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Ne2c8b8eb54bb42478b623df98662e2b4"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group A] expect: subsumed by PartSolidPulmonaryNodule. The condition-versus-subtype case. The subtype is defined, so nobody authors it twice and the component requirement attaches to it automatically.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N6981e70f214b4bcf8ae420938bc9a4bc">
