    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/hasComponent"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/MuralNodule"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E1_ScopeDoesNotTravelAlongContainedIn">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E1 [EXPECT UNRELATED to its pair - neither equivalent nor a subclass of it]: a finding scoped to the kidney</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. Deliberate negative. The kidney reaches the abdomen only through Contained_In, and scope congruence chases partOf alone, so this must NOT classify under a class scoped to the abdomen. If the two ever merge, containedIn has leaked into the partOf family and a scope claim can travel along a location link. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Nc4226c6af70e445b8be25a5517c2f252"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: NOT subsumed by E2, which is expected to stay separate. Deliberate negative. The kidney reaches the abdomen only through Contained_In, and scope congruence chases partOf alone, so this must NOT classify under a class scoped to the abdomen. If the two ever merge, containedIn has leaked into the partOf family and a scope claim can travel along a location link.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
