  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/B3_RibFractureWithChronicAcuity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE B3 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: a rib fracture reported as chronic</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. PulmonaryNodule narrows margin to smooth, lobulated, irregular, spiculated. Narrowing at the point of use is an allValuesFrom axiom rather than an edge property, so a reasoner enforces it. This is the FHIR-profile behaviour named in 02-data-element.md, made checkable. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Na4a1aeafc3ff402d9a8c408ab5c151cc"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group B] expect: unsatisfiable. PulmonaryNodule narrows margin to smooth, lobulated, irregular, spiculated. Narrowing at the point of use is an allValuesFrom axiom rather than an edge property, so a reasoner enforces it. This is the FHIR-profile behaviour named in 02-data-element.md, made checkable.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E3_ScopeTravelsAlongLocalGapFill">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E3 [EXPECT SUBCLASS of an existing class - yellow row in SubClass Of, moves in the tree when the dropdown is set to Inferred]: a finding scoped to the lung parenchyma</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. RadLex gives lung parenchyma exactly one edge, IS_A parenchyma, and never connects it to the lung. A local gap-fill partOf edge supplies that. If this stops classifying under E4, the gap-fill has been lost and everything scoped to lung parenchyma has quietly detached from the lung. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N61a105581236406394347e931f4c993f"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: subsumed by E4. RadLex gives lung parenchyma exactly one edge, IS_A parenchyma, and never connects it to the lung. A local gap-fill partOf edge supplies that. If this stops classifying under E4, the gap-fill has been lost and everything scoped to lung parenchyma has quietly detached from the lung.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
