    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The 30 mm boundary is carried as disjointness, not as a size condition. See DECISIONS.md D-07 for why the criterion itself is an annotation. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N8ac07dfff364471ba3a51f729d844dcd"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group B] expect: unsatisfiable. The 30 mm boundary is carried as disjointness, not as a size condition. See DECISIONS.md D-07 for why the criterion itself is an annotation.</cde:designNote>
