  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/B6_SimpleCystWithMuralNodule">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE B6 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: a simple cyst with a mural nodule</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The conditional actually bites. SimpleCyst fixes composition to cystic; the mural nodule forces the same cyst to be a ComplexCyst, whose composition is mixed cystic and solid. hasComposition is functional (D-02) and the two values are disjoint, so the contradiction surfaces. Note this needed three separate decisions to work: functional componentOf, functional hasComposition, and disjoint values. Remove any one and this probe goes white. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N42e805a33f484b37b4fee765e04a0a2c"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group B] expect: unsatisfiable. The conditional actually bites. SimpleCyst fixes composition to cystic; the mural nodule forces the same cyst to be a ComplexCyst, whose composition is mixed cystic and solid. hasComposition is functional (D-02) and the two values are disjoint, so the contradiction surfaces. Note this needed three separate decisions to work: functional componentOf, functional hasComposition, and disjoint values. Remove any one and this probe goes white.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N11db17d0c69a499789593a10c5f98aa8">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/mayProgressTo"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/RenalCyst"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/D1_FindingClassWithNoAnatomicAnchor">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE D1 [EXPECT CONSISTENT and nothing further - stays where it is, no yellow rows]: a finding class with no anatomic anchor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The lint rules that replace inheritance are not axioms. Nothing here is contradictory, and no reasoner will object to a class with no location, no pattern applied, or an element authored twice. Those checks live in scripts/spec.py lint() and run at authoring time, which is exactly what the pattern decision commits to: consistency by generation and linting rather than by inheritance. D1 staying white is the point. Knowing where a constraint cannot live is the difference between a rule and a hope. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N0832409278b048cc9151268f450d6be0"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group D] expect: SATISFIABLE - expected to stay white. The lint rules that replace inheritance are not axioms. Nothing here is contradictory, and no reasoner will object to a class with no location, no pattern applied, or an element authored twice. Those checks live in scripts/spec.py lint() and run at authoring time, which is exactly what the pattern decision commits to: consistency by generation and linting rather than by inheritance. D1 staying white is the point. Knowing where a constraint cannot live is the difference between a rule and a hope.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Na29819c82cd94170a0747a63c3d4262f">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="Nfe7633003c1645d3a8e5ea9f7c6cbb60"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
